# Presentation Studio

Default native editable PPTX workflow. Do not call create_presentation or generate_presentation: those legacy tools do not implement this source-first workflow.

Inputs:
- Mode: {{mode}}
- Language: {{language}}
- Visual style: {{visual_style}}
- Palette: {{palette}}
- Source path: {{source_path}}
- Company template: {{template_path}}
- Output directory: {{output_dir}}

Resolve mode from the user's intent. Creating from DOCX/PDF is create. Use edit for revisions/translations of a source PPTX unless the user explicitly asks for a new deck. A company design supplied for new content is template. Never merge independent source decks or replace their template without instruction.

## New decks (catalog-v1)

1. Project defaults to {artifactDir}/presentation-studio. Run `node {baseDir}/scripts/prepare_project.mjs --project-dir "<project dir>" --language "<resolved language>" --palette auto --title "<deck title>"` and add `--source "<source DOCX/PPTX>"` when applicable. It combines preflight.mjs and bootstrap, extracts original figures and returns exact paths and image-analysis batches. Never install packages or inspect implementation code to discover the API.
2. Read `{baseDir}/references/catalog-authoring.md` once, plus the scaffold plan and extracted source-asset manifest. This guide is sufficient for ordinary new decks; do not read SKILL.md plus all other design references as a prerequisite. Use existing attachment text; read only missing/truncated source sections. For PDF sources also inspect evidence figures with read_pdf_visual. For extracted DOCX/PPTX figures, use analyze_image with paths batches of up to five (three concurrent), a common prompt and original files. Never run one model/tool round trip per image or shell-resize originals.
3. Write the complete presentation-plan.json once, preserving sourceAssetManifests. Include audience, purpose, coreMessage, narrative stakes/resolution, evidence register, styleRoute and each slide's role/intent/takeaway/evidenceRefs and typed content. Choose one designFamily (business/technology/research). Use real branching flow, mechanisms, comparisons and charts where they explain the content. Keep original figures in the actual PPTX, especially dense diagrams and evidence. Use image-wide for dense figures; native redraws supplement originals, never replace them. Account for every figure via reuse or individually reviewed sourceVisualReview.exclusions. No fabricated claims or numbers. Keep technical detail in notes without losing required visible evidence. Respect requested slide count.
4. Run `node {baseDir}/scripts/build_and_qa.mjs --project-dir "<project dir>"` directly: it validates plan/schema/content/source figures/capacities before compilation, then renders and measures the PPTX. Separate validation is not required; `node {baseDir}/scripts/validate_plan.mjs --project-dir "<project dir>"` is available only when diagnosing a failure. The compiler rejects overflow without truncating or shrinking. Patch only reported fields/slides, not the entire plan. Keep source quantities and qualifications; switch to a wider layout or split where allowed. Do not reread the whole catalog after each error.
5. Read visual-review-queue.json and inspect every PNG via analyze_image paths batches of up to five, max_dimension: 960, with one common concise review prompt. These images are already rendered; do not reconvert the PDF through read_pdf_visual for the same review. Assess hierarchy, diagrams, source readability, clipping, contrast and factual meaning. Use higher-resolution crops for unclear labels. Keep successful reviews and retry only failed pages. Collect blocking fixes in one patch/rebuild, then review changed pages; shared theme changes require reviewing all affected pages. Never count failed requests as passed. If blocked, deliver the built stage draft and state the missing verification rather than silently starting over.
6. Deliver the exact newly built versioned PPTX, editable source directory and qa-report.json. Do not overwrite an earlier version. A successful build alone is not proof of good visual quality. Report limitations honestly.

For a bespoke design that catalog geometry cannot express, read SKILL.md and references/design-system.md, references/slide-types.md, references/pitfalls.md and references/pptxgenjs.md as needed. references/narrative-and-quality.md and references/style-routing.md are additional guidance, not mandatory rereads for catalog decks. Do not mix modules and catalog content or switch to modules merely to bypass overflow.

## Existing decks and templates

Run `node {baseDir}/scripts/preflight.mjs` and read `{baseDir}/SKILL.md` plus references/editing.md for edits, references/template-library.md for new content in an existing template. Keep source-deck edits and translations on the preservation workflow; never bootstrap them as new catalog decks. Translation uses office_translation inspect/apply preserving masters, slide order, theme, images and native objects. Generic 优化PPT requests include real visual improvement: preserve facts/count/order, improve hierarchy/typography/position. Only explicit content-only/original-format requests freeze the layout. Use native-edit.mjs inventory, compose_native_edit.mjs and build_edit.mjs, followed by inspect_edit.mjs on the actual rendered candidate. For template-v1 mode import_template.mjs preserves the company design and uses reviewed native content bindings. Render before/after; a different palette or valid XML does not prove improvement. Inspect every rendered page and identify any incomplete visual QA.
